# Mod uploads live on ai-pipeline

When the user names a Nexus/Vortex mod folder or archive (e.g. `FallUI - Inventory-48758-2-2-1-1666954336`), **inspect it on the production host** — do not search the local Windows workspace.

## Where

| Path | Contents |
|------|----------|
| `/root/Source/transynth/data/uploads/mod/` | Uploaded `.esp/.esm/.esl/.zip/.7z/.rar` |
| `_extracted_{hash}/` under that dir | Unpacked tree for an import |
| `_localize_{hash}/{lang}/` | Localized deltas after export |
| Inside container | same tree at `/app/data/uploads/mod/` |

Host: **ai-pipeline** (SSH via WSL). Prefer absolute `/root/...` — `~` can expand wrong depending on shell.

## How to inspect

```bash
# List / find by name or Nexus id
wsl -e bash -lc "ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=10 ai-pipeline 'ls /root/Source/transynth/data/uploads/mod | grep -i FallUI'"

# Archive listing (cd first — spaces in filenames break remote argv)
wsl -e bash -lc 'ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=10 ai-pipeline "cd /root/Source/transynth/data/uploads/mod && 7z l FallUI*.rar"'
```

If PowerShell eats nested quotes, put the remote commands in a small `.sh`, copy it, and run that (see `.cursor/skills/ai-pipeline/SKILL.md`).

## What to expect

- Many UI/MCM mods have **no** `.esp/.esm/.esl` — only BA2, Interface/MCM translation txt, SWF, etc. Those still belong in this pipeline (MCM / Interface / BA2 paths).
- Code that assumes a plugin always exists is incomplete; check `registerArchiveFile` and MCM/Interface discovery before concluding “not a mod”.

## Do not

- Recurse the local `C:\Users\...` disk for Vortex-style folder names.
- Assume the archive is missing because it is not in the git checkout.
